The root cause here is that the core never tells the instruction‐cache or the external‐fetch logic to shut off when the hart is in debug mode. In Ibex the two places where instructions normally come from are (1) the on‐chip I$ (instantiated in ibex_if_stage.sv and implemented in ibex_icache.sv) and (2) the external fetch interface (ibex_ext_ifetch.sv). Both of these need to be explicitly gated when debug_mode_i is high, and the top‐level core (ibex_core.sv) must carry the debug signal down.

Accordingly, the four modules you’ll most likely need to touch are:

1) hw/ibex/core/rtl/ibex_if_stage.sv – where the I$ is instantiated and one would insert a debug_mode bypass  
2) hw/ibex/core/rtl/ibex_icache.sv – where the cache itself needs to ignore requests in debug  
3) hw/ibex/core/rtl/ibex_ext_ifetch.sv – the fallback fetch path for debug must also be enabled/disabled here  
4) hw/ibex/core/rtl/ibex_core.sv – to ensure the debug_mode_i signal is propagated down into the fetch logic  

```  
hw/ibex/core/rtl/ibex_if_stage.sv  
hw/ibex/core/rtl/ibex_icache.sv  
hw/ibex/core/rtl/ibex_ext_ifetch.sv  
hw/ibex/core/rtl/ibex_core.sv  
```
