│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│  1 Problem summary                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ The issue is that instruction caching remains enabled while the    │
│ core is in debug mode.                                             │
│ That can cause incorrect behavior (e.g., stale/incorrect           │
│ instructions being served) because debug execution should not      │
│ populate/use the normal instruction cache path the same way as     │
│ normal execution.                                                  │
│                                                                    │
│  2 Where it occurs                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ From the provided context, the key connection is in:               │
│                                                                    │
│  • rtl/ibex_core.sv (IF stage instantiation)                       │
│     • icache_enable is passed directly to IF stage:                │
│                                                                    │
│     .icache_enable_i       (icache_enable),                        │
│                                                                    │
│     • debug_mode is also available in this same instantiation:     │
│                                                                    │
│     .debug_mode_i   (debug_mode),                                  │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ So the bug is that icache_enable is not masked off when debug_mode │
│ is active.                                                         │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Best practices for the fix                                      │
│                                                                    │
│  • Keep change minimal and localized.                              │
│  • Reuse existing debug signal (debug_mode) rather than adding new │
│    state.                                                          │
│  • Avoid interface churn (no module port changes unless            │
│    necessary).                                                     │
│  • Make behavior explicit in code with a short comment.            │
│                                                                    │
│  4 Fix approach                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ Gate instruction-cache enable with ~debug_mode when wiring IF      │
│ stage:                                                             │
│                                                                    │
│  • Before: icache_enable_i = icache_enable                         │
│  • After:  icache_enable_i = icache_enable & ~debug_mode           │
│                                                                    │
│ This ensures cache is effectively disabled while in debug mode,    │
│ matching expected upstream behavior.                               │
│                                                                    │
