│    (.debug_mode_i(debug_mode)).                                    │
│  • But cache enable is passed through unchanged as                 │
│    .icache_enable_i(icache_enable).                                │
│                                                                    │
│ So IF/cache logic can still consider cache enabled during debug    │
│ mode.                                                              │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Best practices for the fix                                      │
│                                                                    │
│  • Keep change minimal and local.                                  │
│  • Reuse existing control signal (debug_mode) rather than adding   │
│    new state.                                                      │
│  • Match upstream intent: cache must be effectively disabled in    │
│    debug mode.                                                     │
│  • Avoid modifying unrelated behavior or interfaces.               │
│                                                                    │
│  4 How to fix                                                      │
│                                                                    │
│ Gate the IF-stage cache-enable input with ~debug_mode at the core  │
│ integration point:                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│  • Change:                                                         │
│     • .icache_enable_i(icache_enable)                              │
│  • To:                                                             │
│     • .icache_enable_i(icache_enable & ~debug_mode)                │
│                                                                    │
│ This ensures instruction cache is not used while in debug mode.    │
