│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│  1 Problem summary                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ The issue reports inconsistent PLRU behavior for CMO_PREFETCH when │
│ prefetch_updt_plru == 1:                                           │
│                                                                    │
│  • On hit: PLRU is not updated.                                    │
│  • On miss/refill: PLRU is updated (when refill response is        │
│    received).                                                      │
│                                                                    │
│ This inconsistency is real based on current wiring: prefetch-based │
│ PLRU update is explicitly handled in miss/refill path, but not in  │
│ hit path.                                                          │
│                                                                    │
│  2 Where it occurs                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│  • In hpdcache_miss_handler.sv, refill path already gates PLRU     │
│    update with:                                                    │
│     • cfg_prefetch_updt_sel_victim_i and prefetch metadata.        │
│  • In hpdcache_ctrl.sv, hit-time PLRU update is driven by          │
│    st1_req_updt_sel_victim into hpdcache_memctrl:                  │
│     • .dir_updt_sel_victim_i (st1_req_updt_sel_victim)             │
│  • However, hpdcache_ctrl currently has no prefetch-PLRU config    │
│    input, so hit path cannot honor the same prefetch policy.       │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Best practices for the fix                                      │
│                                                                    │
│  • Keep behavior configurable and consistent across hit and miss   │
│    paths.                                                          │
│  • Avoid touching unrelated logic.                                 │
│  • Keep interface changes minimal and explicit (top -> ctrl        │
│    propagation).                                                   │
│  • Preserve existing non-prefetch replacement behavior by OR-ing   │
│    only the missing prefetch-hit policy.                           │
│                                                                    │
│  4 Fix approach                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  • Add a config input to hpdcache_ctrl:                            │
│    cfg_prefetch_updt_sel_victim_i.                                 │
│  • In hpdcache_ctrl, include prefetch-hit update condition in      │
│    dir_updt_sel_victim_i:                                          │
│     • st1_req_updt_sel_victim | (cfg_prefetch_updt_sel_victim_i &  │
│       st1_req_is_cmo_prefetch)                                     │
│  • Wire this new control from top-level hpdcache.sv using existing │
│    cfg_prefetch_updt_plru_i.                                       │
│                                                                    │
│ This makes CMO_PREFETCH PLRU update policy consistent between hit  │
│ and miss when config is enabled.                                   │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
