╭─ Patch Generation ─────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│  1 Problem summary                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ The issue reports inconsistent PLRU behavior for CMO_PREFETCH when │
│ prefetch_updt_plru == 1:                                           │
│                                                                    │
│  • On prefetch hit: PLRU is not updated.                           │
│  • On prefetch miss: PLRU is updated later during refill response. │
│                                                                    │
│ That inconsistency is real and comes from different update paths.  │
│                                                                    │
│  2 Where it happens                                                │
│                                                                    │
│ From the provided code:                                            │
│                                                                    │
│  • In hpdcache_miss_handler.sv, PLRU update on refill is           │
│    explicitly handled through:                                     │
│     • refill_updt_sel_victim_o = ... (~is_prefetch |               │
│       cfg_prefetch_updt_sel_victim_i);                             │
│     • so prefetch miss can update PLRU when enabled.               │
│  • In hpdcache_ctrl.sv, the directory/memctrl PLRU update input is │
│    currently:                                                      │
│     • .dir_updt_sel_victim_i (st1_req_updt_sel_victim)             │
│  • This hit-path signal does not include CMO_PREFETCH accesses,    │
│    which is why prefetch hits skip PLRU update.                    │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Best practices for the fix                                      │
│                                                                    │
│  • Keep behavior consistent between hit and miss paths for the     │
│    same request class.                                             │
│  • Minimize changes and avoid touching unrelated logic.            │
│  • Avoid introducing new state or broad control rewrites.          │
│  • Keep synthesis-safe combinational logic and preserve existing   │
│    interfaces unless strictly necessary.                           │
│                                                                    │
│  4 How to fix                                                      │
│                                                                    │
│ Adjust the hit-path PLRU update condition in hpdcache_ctrl.sv so   │
│ that CMO_PREFETCH requests also request victim-selection update in │
│ the directory control path.                                        │
│ This aligns hit behavior with miss behavior and resolves the       │
│ reported inconsistency.                                            │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                    Phase 2: FIX IMPLEMENTATION                     │
│                                                                    │
│ ┏━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┓ │
