│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│  1 Problem summary                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ The RVFI probe port csr_pmpaddr_q_i expects an unpacked array of   │
│ 32-bit entries:                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  • input logic [31:0] csr_pmpaddr_q_i[PMP_MAX_REGIONS]             │
│                                                                    │
│ But the wrapper currently connects it directly to:                 │
│                                                                    │
│  • core_i.cs_registers_i.pmp_addr_rdata                            │
│                                                                    │
│ which is an unpacked array of PMP_ADDR_WIDTH entries (e.g. 30 bits │
│ when PMP_GRANULARITY=3).                                           │
│ This causes strict type mismatch in Xcelium and also leads to      │
│ incorrect RVFI CSR visibility for PMP address values.              │
│                                                                    │
│  2 Where it occurs                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ In bhv/cv32e40s_wrapper.sv, the problematic connection is here:    │
│                                                                    │
│  • .csr_pmpaddr_q_i ( core_i.cs_registers_i.pmp_addr_rdata )       │
│                                                                    │
│ (from provided Location #1)                                        │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Best practices for the fix                                      │
│                                                                    │
│  • Keep RTL behavior unchanged; only adapt probe wiring.           │
│  • Avoid broad refactors; apply minimal targeted conversion at     │
│    connection point.                                               │
│  • Make conversion explicit so strict simulators (Xcelium) accept  │
│    it.                                                             │
│  • Preserve array structure and index mapping 1:1.                 │
│                                                                    │
│  4 Fix approach                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ Explicitly build a 32-bit unpacked array assignment pattern in the │
│ wrapper connection, casting each PMP entry to 32 bits.             │
│ This resolves type compatibility and ensures RVFI receives 32-bit  │
│ CSR data elements.                                                 │
│                                                                    │
