│                                                                    │
│  1 Problem summary                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ The RVFI wrapper connects csr_pmpaddr_q_i to                       │
│ core_i.cs_registers_i.pmp_addr_rdata.                              │
│ For non-zero PMP granularity (PMP_GRANULARITY > 0), pmp_addr_rdata │
│ is narrower than 32 bits (PMP_ADDR_WIDTH), while RVFI expects a    │
│ 32-bit array per PMP entry.                                        │
│ This causes a strict type mismatch in Xcelium and also leads to    │
│ incorrect RVFI PMP CSR value reporting.                            │
│                                                                    │
│  2 Where it occurs                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│  • File: bhv/cv32e40s_wrapper.sv                                   │
│  • Connection block around:                                        │
│     • .csr_pmpaddr_n_i ( core_i.cs_registers_i.pmp_addr_n )        │
│     • .csr_pmpaddr_q_i ( core_i.cs_registers_i.pmp_addr_rdata )    │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Best practices for the fix                                      │
│                                                                    │
│  • Keep RVFI probe interfaces type-consistent (32-bit CSR view).   │
│  • Avoid connecting reduced internal storage representation        │
│    directly to architecturally-visible tracing interfaces.         │
│  • Apply the smallest possible change in wrapper plumbing to       │
│    preserve behavior elsewhere.                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  4 Fix approach                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ Use a 32-bit compatible PMP address signal for RVFI q probing      │
│ instead of pmp_addr_rdata (which is width-reduced for granularity  │
│ handling).                                                         │
│ pmp_addr_n is already connected to a 32-bit RVFI input and is      │
│ type-compatible, so reusing it for csr_pmpaddr_q_i resolves the    │
│ compilation mismatch and avoids feeding truncated-width data into  │
│ RVFI.                                                              │
