│                                                                    │
│  1 Problem summary                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ The RVFI wrapper connects core_i.cs_registers_i.pmp_addr_rdata     │
│ directly to RVFI port csr_pmpaddr_q_i.                             │
│ When PMP granularity G != 0, pmp_addr_rdata is narrower            │
│ (PMP_ADDR_WIDTH, e.g. 30 bits for G=3) than RVFI’s expected 32-bit │
│ CSR element width.                                                 │
│ Xcelium enforces strict type compatibility for unpacked arrays and │
│ fails elaboration.                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│  2 Where it occurs                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ In bhv/cv32e40s_wrapper.sv, at the RVFI instantiation around:      │
│                                                                    │
│  • .csr_pmpaddr_q_i ( core_i.cs_registers_i.pmp_addr_rdata )       │
│                                                                    │
│ This is exactly the incompatible connection reported in the issue. │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Best practices for fix                                          │
│                                                                    │
│  • Keep RVFI-visible CSR values at architectural width (32-bit for │
│    RV32 CSRs).                                                     │
│  • Avoid changing core CSR storage width (it is                    │
│    implementation-driven and valid).                               │
│  • Apply explicit widening at the wrapper boundary to avoid        │
│    tool-dependent implicit behavior.                               │
│  • Keep change minimal and localized.                              │
│                                                                    │
│  4 Fix approach                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ Explicitly zero-extend each PMP address entry from pmp_addr_rdata  │
│ to 32 bits in the wrapper connection to RVFI.                      │
│ This resolves strict type-checking and ensures RVFI observes       │
│ correct 32-bit CSR values.                                         │
