│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│  1 Problem statement                                               │
│                                                                    │
│ popcount.sv currently has inconsistent support for INPUT_WIDTH=1:  │
│                                                                    │
│  • The code has a special branch for INPUT_WIDTH == 1, implying    │
│    support exists.                                                 │
│  • But the header comment says only INPUT_WIDTH >= 2 is legal.     │
│  • More importantly, for INPUT_WIDTH=1, this declaration becomes   │
│    invalid:                                                        │
│                                                                    │
│     logic [PopcountWidth-2:0] left_child_result,                   │
│     right_child_result;                                            │
│                                                                    │
│    because PopcountWidth = $clog2(1)+1 = 1, so the range becomes   │
│    [-1:0], which can crash tools (as reported for VCS).            │
│                                                                    │
│  2 Where it occurs                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ In src/popcount.sv:                                                │
│                                                                    │
│  • Documentation mismatch in the module description (larger or     │
│    equal 2).                                                       │
│  • Buggy packed range in the internal signal declaration:          │
│     • logic [PopcountWidth-2:0] left_child_result,                 │
│       right_child_result;                                          │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Best practices for the fix                                      │
│                                                                    │
│  • Keep changes minimal and localized.                             │
│  • Ensure all parameter values that are intended to be supported   │
│    produce valid compile-time ranges.                              │
│  • Use a derived localparam for width sizing rather than inline    │
│    “magic” ternaries in many places.                               │
│  • Keep existing behavior unchanged for INPUT_WIDTH > 1.           │
│                                                                    │
│  4 Fix approach                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  • Update the comment to state INPUT_WIDTH >= 1 is legal.          │
│  • Introduce a safe child-width localparam:                        │
│                                                                    │
│     localparam int unsigned ChildPopcountWidth = (INPUT_WIDTH > 1  │
│     ? PopcountWidth - 1 : 1;                                       │
│                                                                    │
│  • Use it for internal child-result signals:                       │
│                                                                    │
│     logic [ChildPopcountWidth-1:0] left_child_result,              │
│     right_child_result;                                            │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ This avoids negative ranges for INPUT_WIDTH=1 while preserving     │
│ previous sizing for wider inputs.                                  │
│                                                                    │
