│                                                                    │
│  1 Problem summary                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ popcount.sv currently claims only INPUT_WIDTH >= 2 is legal, but   │
│ the module has INPUT_WIDTH = 1 as default and explicit generate    │
│ logic for INPUT_WIDTH == 1.                                        │
│ So there is a doc/implementation mismatch.                         │
│                                                                    │
│ More importantly, for INPUT_WIDTH = 1:                             │
│                                                                    │
│  • PopcountWidth = $clog2(1)+1 = 1                                 │
│  • logic [PopcountWidth-2:0] ... becomes logic [-1:0] ...          │
│                                                                    │
│ This is an illegal/negative range and can crash simulators (as     │
│ reported for VCS).                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│  2 Where the bug is                                                │
│                                                                    │
│ In src/popcount.sv:                                                │
│                                                                    │
│  • Comment block says legal width is >= 2 (incorrect now).         │
│  • Declaration:                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│     logic [PopcountWidth-2:0] left_child_result,                   │
│     right_child_result;                                            │
│                                                                    │
│    causes invalid range when PopcountWidth == 1.                   │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Best practices for the fix                                      │
│                                                                    │
│  • Keep parameterized vector widths non-negative and non-zero for  │
│    all legal parameter values.                                     │
│  • Preserve existing recursive structure and behavior for widths   │
│    >= 2.                                                           │
│  • Make documentation consistent with actual supported parameter   │
│    space.                                                          │
│  • Apply a minimal change with no functional regressions.          │
│                                                                    │
│  4 Fix approach                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  • Update description to state INPUT_WIDTH >= 1 is legal.          │
│  • Introduce a safe child-width localparam that clamps minimum     │
│    width to 1:                                                     │
│                                                                    │
│     localparam int unsigned ChildPopcountWidth = (PopcountWidth >  │
│     1) ? (PopcountWidth - 1) : 1;                                  │
│                                                                    │
│  • Use that for child result signals:                              │
│                                                                    │
│     logic [ChildPopcountWidth-1:0] left_child_result,              │
│     right_child_result;                                            │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ This removes negative ranges and keeps correct widths for          │
│ recursive cases.                                                   │
│                                                                    │
