│                                                                    │
│ There is also a documentation mismatch: comments still say only    │
│ widths >=2 are legal.                                              │
│                                                                    │
│  2 Where it occurs                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│  • src/popcount.sv                                                 │
│     • Header comment (legal width statement is outdated).          │
│     • Child result declaration uses PopcountWidth-2:0 directly,    │
│       causing negative range when INPUT_WIDTH=1.                   │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Best practices for the fix                                      │
│                                                                    │
│  • Avoid negative or zero-width packed ranges by introducing a     │
│    guarded localparam for width.                                   │
│  • Keep behavior unchanged for existing supported widths.          │
│  • Keep fix minimal and local to the source module.                │
│  • Align module documentation with actual supported behavior.      │
│                                                                    │
│  4 Fix approach                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  • Add a localparam for child result width:                        │
│     • ChildResultWidth = (PopcountWidth > 1) ? (PopcountWidth - 1) │
│       : 1;                                                         │
│  • Use it in declarations:                                         │
│     • logic [ChildResultWidth-1:0] left_child_result,              │
│       right_child_result;                                          │
│  • Update the module description text from >=2 to >=1.             │
