I walked through the debug‐module’s SBA logic and DMI–register‐file code and convinced myself that the bug lives squarely in the two places where we

  1. track “sberror” in the system-bus–access engine, and 
  2. decode and apply a W1C write to clear it.

Those two units are instantiated by the top-level `dm_ctrl` and hooked into the DMI front-end, so you also need to poke at

  • the DMI-register‐file that exposes “sberror” to the host, and  
  • the top-level controller that wires the write-1-to-clear path through.

The four files that need fixes, in priority order, are:

```  
src/hdl/rv_dm_system_bus_access.sv
src/hdl/rv_dm_dmi_regfile.sv
src/hdl/rv_dm_ctrl.sv
src/hdl/rv_dm_dmi.sv
