Based on the RISC-V Debug Spec, the “DMIRESET” bit in the DTM Control and Status Register (DTMCS) must act as a write-one clear (“W1C”) pulse. Right now we latch it like a normal register bit and it remains set until the CSR is rewritten, which breaks the spec. The logic for this lives in the files defining the DTMCS register itself, the top-level DTM core that wires it up, the DMI interface that drivers reads/writes into that CSR, and the DTM’s FSM which should react to that pulse. These four are the most likely places you’ll have to introduce an auto-clear or pulse-generate for DMIRESET:

```  
src/rtl/dtm_registers.sv
src/rtl/dtm_core.sv
src/rtl/dmi_if.sv
src/rtl/dtm_fsm.sv
```
