│                                                                    │
│ The SPI host FSM mishandles a CSID change between commands. When a │
│ new command arrives for a different CSID than the previous         │
│ command, the FSM incorrectly routes through WaitIdle instead of    │
│ the dedicated CSBSwitch path. As a result, it effectively skips    │
│ the first command after a CSID switch, because the FSM does not    │
│ properly account for the extra switching delay required before     │
│ accepting the new command.                                         │
│                                                                    │
