I looked at the error (“cannot open include file axi_flat.svh” and “undefined macro AXI_FLATTEN_MASTER”) and traced it back to the Vivado‐target build of Occamy (the `occamy_vcu128` make target). The two immediate hotspots are:

  1. The SystemVerilog top itself (`occamy_xilinx.sv`) is including `axi_flat.svh` but no such file exists in the repo / the include path is wrong.  
  2. The occamy‐specific Makefile (and the Vivado TCL script it invokes) must be told where to find the SVH file (and ship it into the project).

As a result, you’ll need to:

  • Fix the `include` in `occamy_xilinx.sv` (or adjust the path).  
  • Add/point the missing `axi_flat.svh` file into the search path.  
  • Update the occamy Makefile so that it passes the SV include directory to Vivado.  
  • Update the Vivado TCL script so it actually adds the new SVH file to the project.  

Below is my pick of the four files you will almost certainly need to touch. Ordered from most‐critical (the place that fails first) to least:

```text
hw/system/occamy/src/occamy_xilinx.sv
hw/system/occamy/Makefile
hw/system/occamy/scripts/vivado.tcl
Makefile
